2023-07-10","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312523184697/0001193125-23-184697-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2023-07-10","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312523184693/0001193125-23-184693-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2023-07-10","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312523184683/0001193125-23-184683-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2023-07-10","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312523184653/0001193125-23-184653-index.htm","tone":"warn"}],"summary":{"sentences":["GEN Restaurant Group, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Retail-Eating  Places\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 2 years.","It reported $216.7m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, down 6.0% against the same quarter a year earlier.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($11.1m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Growth has been positive in 7 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526224023/0001193125-26-224023-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-224023"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $11.1m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526224023/0001193125-26-224023-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-224023"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 6.0% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526224023/0001193125-26-224023-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-224023"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-13.4% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526224023/0001193125-26-224023-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-224023"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $5.0m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526224023/0001193125-26-224023-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-224023"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 6.4% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526224023/0001193125-26-224023-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-224023"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.8% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000213772526000003/0002137725-26-000003-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -21.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.21,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.06,"current_display":"-6.0%","threshold_display":"-21.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id"